1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:04,538
Chapter 10 Here the two, I have recorded in

2
00:00:04,539 --> 00:00:09,139
detail the events of my insignificant existence.

3
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:14,500
To the first 10 years of my life, I have given almost as many chapters.

4
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:17,959
But this is not to be a regular autobiography.

5
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:21,791
I am only bound to invoke memory where I know her

6
00:00:21,792 --> 00:00:24,520
responses will possess some degree of interest.

7
00:00:25,579 --> 00:00:30,739
Therefore, I now pass a space of eight years, almost in silence.

8
00:00:31,850 --> 00:00:36,219
A few lines only are necessary to keep up the links of connection.

9
00:00:38,319 --> 00:00:42,500
When the typhus fever had fulfilled its mission of devastation at lowered,

10
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:45,819
it gradually disappeared from thence.

11
00:00:46,825 --> 00:00:49,441
But not till its virulence and the number of its

12
00:00:49,442 --> 00:00:52,421
victims had drawn public attention on the school.

13
00:00:53,799 --> 00:01:00,040
Inquiry was made into the origin of the scourge, and by degrees, various facts

14
00:01:00,090 --> 00:01:04,559
came out which excited public indignation in a high degree.

15
00:01:05,469 --> 00:01:10,420
The unhealthy nature of the site, the quantity and quality of the children's

16
00:01:10,421 --> 00:01:15,420
food, the brackish, fetid water used in its preparation.

17
00:01:16,399 --> 00:01:21,820
The pupils wretched clothing and accommodations, all these things were discovered.

18
00:01:22,389 --> 00:01:26,620
And the discovery produced a result, mortifying to Mr. Brocklehurst,

19
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:28,979
but beneficial to the institution.

20
00:01:31,329 --> 00:01:37,760
Several wealthy and benevolent individuals in the county subscribed, largely for the

21
00:01:37,761 --> 00:01:41,180
erection of a more convenient building in a better situation.

22
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:47,420
New regulations were made, improvements in diet and clothing introduced.

23
00:01:48,319 --> 00:01:51,899
The funds of the school were entrusted to the management of a committee.

24
00:01:53,719 --> 00:01:59,479
Mr. Brocklehurst, who, from his wealth and family connections, could not be

25
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:02,940
overlooked, still retained the post of treasurer.

26
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:07,299
But he was aided in the discharge of his duties by

27
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:11,420
gentleman of rather more enlarged and sympathizing minds.

28
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:17,739
His office of inspector, too, was shared by those who knew how to combine reason

29
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:22,799
with strictness, comfort with economy, compassion with uprightness.

30
00:02:24,069 --> 00:02:30,139
The school, thus improved, became in time a truly useful and noble institution.

31
00:02:31,450 --> 00:02:36,079
I remained an inmate of its walls after its regeneration for eight years,

32
00:02:36,819 --> 00:02:38,860
six as pupil and two as teacher.

33
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:43,879
And in both capacities, I bear my testimony to its value and importance.

34
00:02:45,170 --> 00:02:48,596
During these eight years, my life was uniform,

35
00:02:48,597 --> 00:02:51,921
but not unhappy, because it was not inactive.

36
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:04,219
I had for some of my studies and a desire to excel in all, together with a great

37
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:09,479
delight in pleasing my teachers, especially such as I loved, urged me on.

38
00:03:11,184 --> 00:03:14,219
I availed myself fully of the advantages offered me.

39
00:03:15,274 --> 00:03:18,659
In time, I rose to be the first girl of the first class.

40
00:03:19,670 --> 00:03:22,664
Then, I was invested with the office of teacher,

41
00:03:22,665 --> 00:03:25,861
which I discharged with zeal for two years.

42
00:03:26,229 --> 00:03:28,260
But at the end of that time, I altered.

43
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:33,121
Miss Temple, through all changes, had thus

44
00:03:33,122 --> 00:03:36,740
far continued super-intendent of the seminary.

45
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:41,180
To her instruction, I owed the best part of my requirements.

46
00:03:42,219 --> 00:03:45,559
Her friendship and society had been my continual solace.

47
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:51,299
She had stood me in the stead of mother, governess, and latterly companion.

48
00:03:52,569 --> 00:03:57,191
At this period, she married, removed with her husband, a

49
00:03:57,191 --> 00:04:01,700
clergyman, an excellent man, almost worthy of such a wife.

50
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:06,819
To a distant county, and consequently, was lost to me.

51
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:11,120
From the day she left, I was no longer the same.

52
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:15,632
With her was gone every settled feeling, every association

53
00:04:15,634 --> 00:04:18,799
that had made lowered in some degree, a home to me.

54
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:24,040
I had imbibed from her something of her nature and much of her habits,

55
00:04:25,069 --> 00:04:27,879
more harmonious thoughts, what seemed better

56
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:31,360
regulated feelings had become the inmates of my mind.

57
00:04:32,579 --> 00:04:35,280
I had given in allegiance to duty and order.

58
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,200
I was quiet.

59
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:39,260
I believed I was content.

60
00:04:40,049 --> 00:04:43,342
To the eyes of others, usually even to my own,

61
00:04:43,343 --> 00:04:47,081
I appeared a disciplined and subdued character.

62
00:04:47,534 --> 00:04:50,629
But destiny, in the shape of the reverend

63
00:04:50,629 --> 00:04:54,740
Mr. Nazmuth, came between me and Miss Temple.

64
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:58,163
I saw her in her traveling dress, step into a

65
00:04:58,164 --> 00:05:00,960
post-shays, shortly after the marriage ceremony.

66
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:05,959
I watched the shares mount the hill and disappear beyond its brow, and then

67
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:11,559
retired to my own room, and their spent in solitude, the greatest part of the half

68
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:14,760
holiday, granted in honour of the occasion.

69
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:18,559
I walked about the chamber most of the time.

70
00:05:19,709 --> 00:05:25,659
I imagined myself only to be regretting my loss, and thinking how to repair it.

71
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:30,860
But when my reflections were concluded, and I looked up and found that the

72
00:05:30,861 --> 00:05:37,100
afternoon was gone, and evening far advanced, another discovery dawned on me.

73
00:05:37,639 --> 00:05:42,059
Namely, that in the interval I had undergone a transforming process,

74
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:48,120
that my mind had put off all it had borrowed of Miss Temple, or rather that

75
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:52,479
she had taken with her, the serene atmosphere I had been breathing in her

76
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:57,558
vicinity, and that now I was left in my natural element,

77
00:05:57,558 --> 00:06:01,459
and beginning to feel the stirring of old emotions.

78
00:06:02,725 --> 00:06:09,661
It did not seem as if a prop were withdrawn, but rather as if a motive were gone.

79
00:06:09,944 --> 00:06:13,389
It was not the power to be tranquil which had failed

80
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:16,399
me, but the reason for tranquility was no more.

81
00:06:17,319 --> 00:06:20,520
My world had for some years been in lowered.

82
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:24,280
My experience had been of its rules and systems.

83
00:06:25,329 --> 00:06:31,299
Now I remembered that the real world was wide, and that varied field of hopes and

84
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:37,639
fears, of sensations and excitements awaited those who had courage to go forth

85
00:06:38,290 --> 00:06:43,579
into its expanse, to seek real knowledge of life amidst its perils.

86
00:06:44,465 --> 00:06:47,899
I went to my window, opened it, and looked out.

87
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:53,940
There were the two wings of the building, there was the garden, there were the

88
00:06:53,941 --> 00:06:57,260
skirts of lowered, there was the hilly horizon.

89
00:06:58,870 --> 00:07:03,479
My eye passed all other objects to rest on those most remote, the blue peaks.

90
00:07:04,479 --> 00:07:06,520
It was those I longed to some mount.

91
00:07:07,309 --> 00:07:12,159
All within their boundary of rock and heath seemed prison ground, exile limits.

92
00:07:13,319 --> 00:07:18,780
I traced the white road winding round the base of one mountain, and vanishing in a

93
00:07:18,781 --> 00:07:22,579
gorge between two, how I longed to follow it farther.

94
00:07:24,010 --> 00:07:27,500
I recalled the time when I had travelled that very road in a coach.

95
00:07:28,579 --> 00:07:31,059
I remembered descending that hill at twilight.

96
00:07:32,290 --> 00:07:37,360
An age seemed to have elapsed since the day which brought me first to low wood,

97
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:39,819
and I had never quitted it since.

98
00:07:41,219 --> 00:07:43,920
My vacations had all been spent at school.

99
00:07:44,870 --> 00:07:49,016
Mrs. Reed had never sent for me to Gateshead, neither

100
00:07:49,018 --> 00:07:52,659
she nor any of her family had ever been to visit me.

101
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:58,139
I had had no communication by letter or message with the outer world.

102
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:05,319
School rules, school duties, school habits and notions, and voices and faces and

103
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:08,222
phrases and costumes and preferences and

104
00:08:08,224 --> 00:08:12,001
antipathies, such was what I knew of existence.

105
00:08:12,569 --> 00:08:15,079
And now I felt that it was not enough.

106
00:08:16,159 --> 00:08:18,940
I tired of the routine of eight years in one afternoon.

107
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:21,020
I desired liberty.

108
00:08:21,719 --> 00:08:23,500
For liberty I gasped.

109
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,899
For liberty I uttered a prayer.

110
00:08:26,559 --> 00:08:29,620
It seemed scattered on the wind, then faintly blowing.

111
00:08:30,319 --> 00:08:33,520
I abandoned it and framed a humblest supplication.

112
00:08:34,219 --> 00:08:36,180
For change, stimulus.

113
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:41,639
That petition too seemed swept off into vague space.

114
00:08:43,379 --> 00:08:45,940
Then I cried, half desperate.

115
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:48,299
Grumped me at least a new servitude.

116
00:08:49,290 --> 00:08:52,500
Here a bell ringing the hour of supper called me downstairs.

117
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:57,000
I was not free to resume the interrupted chain of my reflections till bedtime.

118
00:08:58,190 --> 00:09:03,799
Even then, a teacher who occupied the same room with me kept me from the subject to

119
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:08,579
which I longed to recur by a prolonged effusion of small talk.

120
00:09:10,799 --> 00:09:13,239
How I wished sleep would silence her.

121
00:09:14,059 --> 00:09:17,174
It seemed as if could I but go back to the idea which

122
00:09:17,174 --> 00:09:19,820
had last entered my mind as I stood at the window.

123
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:23,139
Some inventive suggestion would rise for my relief.

124
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:26,399
Miss Greise snored at last.

125
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:28,559
She was a heavy Welsh woman.

126
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:33,063
Until now her habitual nasal strains had never been

127
00:09:33,064 --> 00:09:36,540
regarded by me in any other light than as a nuisance.

128
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:41,520
Tonight, I hailed the first deep notes with satisfaction.

129
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,860
I was debarrest of interruption.

130
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:47,319
My half-a-face thought instantly revived.

131
00:09:48,139 --> 00:09:49,139
A new servitude.

132
00:09:49,819 --> 00:09:52,540
There is something in that, I soliloquized.

133
00:09:53,319 --> 00:09:55,600
Mentally, be it understood, I did not talk aloud.

134
00:09:56,809 --> 00:10:00,100
I know there is because it does not sound too sweet.

135
00:10:01,090 --> 00:10:05,340
It is not like such words as liberty, excitement, enjoyment.

136
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:09,780
Delightful sounds truly, but no more than sounds for me.

137
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:15,459
And so hollow and fleeting that it is mere waste of time to listen to them.

138
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,440
But servitude.

139
00:10:18,969 --> 00:10:20,090
That must be matter of fact.

140
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:21,700
Anyone may serve.

141
00:10:22,409 --> 00:10:23,610
I have served you eight years.

142
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,979
Now all I want is to serve elsewhere.

143
00:10:26,950 --> 00:10:28,879
Can I not get so much of my own will?

144
00:10:29,739 --> 00:10:30,780
Is not the thing feasible?

145
00:10:31,239 --> 00:10:32,239
Yes.

146
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:32,719
Yes.

147
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,940
The end is not so difficult.

148
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:39,709
If I had only a brain active enough to ferret out the means of attaining it.

149
00:10:41,270 --> 00:10:44,670
I sat up in bed by way of arousing this said brain.

150
00:10:45,610 --> 00:10:46,670
It was a chilly night.

151
00:10:47,370 --> 00:10:49,773
I covered my shoulders with a shawl, and then

152
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:52,649
I proceeded to think again with all my might.

153
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:54,750
What do I want?

154
00:10:55,639 --> 00:10:57,829
A new place in a new house.

155
00:10:58,409 --> 00:11:02,111
Amongst new faces under new circumstances, I want

156
00:11:02,111 --> 00:11:05,149
this because it is of no use wanting anything better.

157
00:11:06,959 --> 00:11:08,790
How do people do to get a new place?

158
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:11,129
They apply to friends, I suppose.

159
00:11:11,829 --> 00:11:12,829
I have no friends.

160
00:11:14,184 --> 00:11:16,947
There are many others who have no friends who must

161
00:11:16,948 --> 00:11:19,750
look about for themselves and be their own helpers.

162
00:11:20,829 --> 00:11:21,989
And what is their resource?

163
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:24,950
I could not tell.

164
00:11:26,069 --> 00:11:27,370
Nothing answered me.

165
00:11:28,569 --> 00:11:31,350
I then ordered my brain to find a response and quickly.

166
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:33,950
It worked and worked faster.

167
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,469
I felt the pulses throb in my head and temples.

168
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:43,329
But for nearly an hour it worked in chaos, and no result came of its efforts.

169
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:48,290
Feverish with vain labour, I got up and took a turn in the room.

170
00:11:49,069 --> 00:11:55,490
Undrew the curtain, noted a star or two, shivered with cold, and again crept to bed.

171
00:11:55,739 --> 00:12:02,390
A kind fairy in my absence had surely dropped the required suggestion on my pillow.

172
00:12:02,899 --> 00:12:06,629
For as I lay down, it came quietly and naturally to my mind.

173
00:12:07,625 --> 00:12:12,770
Those who want situations advertise, you must advertise in the shy herald.

174
00:12:13,909 --> 00:12:14,909
How?

175
00:12:15,370 --> 00:12:17,049
I know nothing about advertising.

176
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:20,049
Replies rose smooth and prompt now.

177
00:12:21,010 --> 00:12:24,590
You must enclose the advertisement and the money to pay for it.

178
00:12:25,165 --> 00:12:30,250
Under a cover directed to the editor of the herald, you must put it the first

179
00:12:30,251 --> 00:12:33,889
opportunity you have into the post at Loton.

180
00:12:34,590 --> 00:12:37,010
Answers must be addressed to J.E.

181
00:12:37,549 --> 00:12:38,549
at the post office there.

182
00:12:39,409 --> 00:12:43,069
You can go and inquire in about a week after you send your letter if any are come

183
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:44,469
and act accordingly.

184
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:49,250
This scheme I went over twice, thrice.

185
00:12:50,110 --> 00:12:51,930
It was then digested in my mind.

186
00:12:52,659 --> 00:12:54,950
I had it in a clear, practical form.

187
00:12:55,739 --> 00:12:57,829
I felt satisfied and fell asleep.

188
00:12:59,049 --> 00:13:00,549
With earliest day, I was up.

189
00:13:01,379 --> 00:13:03,876
I had my advertisement written and closed and

190
00:13:03,877 --> 00:13:06,290
directed before the bell rang to rouse the school.

191
00:13:06,870 --> 00:13:07,870
It ran thus.

192
00:13:09,270 --> 00:13:11,250
A young lady accustomed to tuition.

193
00:13:12,829 --> 00:13:14,469
Had I not been a teacher two years?

194
00:13:16,245 --> 00:13:18,540
Is desirous of meeting with a situation in a

195
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:21,850
private family where the children are under 14?

196
00:13:21,851 --> 00:13:26,041
I thought that, as I was barely 18, it would not do

197
00:13:26,042 --> 00:13:30,690
to undertake the guidance of pupils nearer my own age.

198
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:37,850
She is qualified to teach the usual branches of a good English education,

199
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:41,450
together with French, drawing and music.

200
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:46,382
In those days, reader, this now narrow catalog of

201
00:13:46,384 --> 00:13:50,319
accomplishments would have been held tolerably comprehensive.

202
00:13:51,479 --> 00:13:56,200
Address, J.E., Post Office, Loton, Shire.

203
00:13:57,805 --> 00:14:00,540
This document remained locked in my drawer all day.

204
00:14:02,110 --> 00:14:06,020
After T, I asked leave of the new superintendent to go to Loton.

205
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:09,340
In order to perform some small commissions for myself and one

206
00:14:09,341 --> 00:14:13,520
or two of my fellow teachers, permission was readily granted.

207
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,620
I went.

208
00:14:17,579 --> 00:14:24,001
It was a walk of two miles, and the evening was wet, but the days were still long.

209
00:14:24,579 --> 00:14:30,260
I visited a shop or two, slipped the letter into the Post Office, and came back

210
00:14:30,409 --> 00:14:36,280
through heavy rain with streaming garments, but with a relieved heart.

211
00:14:37,629 --> 00:14:39,559
The succeeding week seemed long.

212
00:14:40,479 --> 00:14:45,739
It came to an end at last, however, like all sublunary things, and once more.

213
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:53,921
Towards the close of a pleasant autumn day, I found myself a foot on the road to Loton.

214
00:14:54,170 --> 00:14:57,865
A picturesque track it was, by the way, lying along the

215
00:14:57,867 --> 00:15:01,159
side of the beck and through the sweetest curves of the day.

216
00:15:02,709 --> 00:15:07,540
But that day, I thought more of the letters that might or might not be

217
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:13,540
awaiting me at the little burg wither I was bound, then of the charms of Lea and Water.

218
00:15:14,649 --> 00:15:19,840
My ostensible errand on this occasion was to get measured for a pair of shoes,

219
00:15:20,790 --> 00:15:22,760
so I discharged that business first.

220
00:15:23,799 --> 00:15:27,168
And when it was done, I stepped across the clean and quiet

221
00:15:27,170 --> 00:15:30,440
little street from the shoemakers to the Post Office.

222
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:35,736
It was kept by an old Dame, who wore horn spectacles

223
00:15:35,736 --> 00:15:39,100
on her nose and black mittens on her hands.

224
00:15:40,379 --> 00:15:42,200
Are there any letters for J.E.?

225
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,200
I asked.

226
00:15:44,030 --> 00:15:48,620
She peered at me over her spectacles, and then she opened a drawer and fumbled

227
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:54,420
among its contents for a long time, so long that my hopes began to falter.

228
00:15:55,579 --> 00:15:59,860
At last, having held a document before her glasses for nearly five minutes,

229
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:04,356
she presented it across the counter, accompanying the

230
00:16:04,358 --> 00:16:07,440
act by another inquisitive and mistrustful glance.

231
00:16:08,434 --> 00:16:09,540
It was for J.E.

232
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,840
Is there only one I demanded?

233
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,680
There are no more, suchy.

234
00:16:16,829 --> 00:16:20,459
And I put it in my pocket and turned my face homeward.

235
00:16:21,299 --> 00:16:22,440
I could not open it then.

236
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:28,219
Rules obliged me to be back by eight, and it was already half past seven.

237
00:16:29,299 --> 00:16:31,600
Various duties awaited me on my arrival.

238
00:16:32,399 --> 00:16:34,920
I had to sit with the girls during their hour of study.

239
00:16:35,709 --> 00:16:39,120
Then it was my turn to read prayers, to see them to bed.

240
00:16:40,159 --> 00:16:42,600
Afterwards, I sucked with the other teachers.

241
00:16:43,459 --> 00:16:46,496
Even when we finally retired for the night, the

242
00:16:46,497 --> 00:16:49,581
inevitable miss-gryce was still my companion.

243
00:16:50,409 --> 00:16:54,319
We had only a short end of candle in our candlestick, and

244
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:57,639
I dreaded lest she should talk till it was all burnt out.

245
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:05,459
Fortunately, however, the heavy supper she had eaten produced a soporific effect.

246
00:17:06,370 --> 00:17:09,280
She was already snoring before I had finished undressing.

247
00:17:10,299 --> 00:17:12,079
There still remained an inch of candle.

248
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,819
I now took out my letter.

249
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:16,579
The seal was an initial F.

250
00:17:17,360 --> 00:17:18,360
I broke it.

251
00:17:18,479 --> 00:17:19,659
The contents were brief.

252
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:26,100
If J.E., who advertised in the sighing shire, herald of last Thursday,

253
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:28,920
possesses the requirements mentioned.

254
00:17:29,829 --> 00:17:34,120
And if she is in a position to give satisfactory references as to character

255
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:40,379
and competency, a situation can be offered her where there is but one pupil,

256
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:48,700
a little girl, under ten years of age, and where the salary is £30 per annum.

257
00:17:50,059 --> 00:17:51,139
J.E.

258
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:58,081
is requested to send references, name, address, and all particulars to the direction.

259
00:17:58,760 --> 00:17:59,379
J.E.

260
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:03,860
Mrs. Fairfax, Thornfield, near Millcoat, Shire.

261
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,399
I examined the document long.

262
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:11,860
The writing was old-fashioned and rather uncertain, like that of an elderly lady.

263
00:18:12,879 --> 00:18:14,659
This circumstance was satisfactory.

264
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:20,100
A private fear had haunted me, that in thus acting for myself,

265
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:25,239
and by my own guidance, I ran the risk of getting into some scrape.

266
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:31,559
And above all things, I wished the result of my endeavours to be respectable,

267
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:33,899
proper, on-regal.

268
00:18:35,590 --> 00:18:40,819
I now felt that an elderly lady was no bad ingredient in the business I had on hand.

269
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:48,200
Mrs. Fairfax, I saw her in a black gown and widow's cap, frigid perhaps,

270
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:49,780
but not uncivil.

271
00:18:50,364 --> 00:18:54,680
A model of elderly English respectability, Thornfield.

272
00:18:55,545 --> 00:19:00,379
That doubtless was the name of her house, a neat, orderly spot I was sure,

273
00:19:01,219 --> 00:19:04,680
though I failed in my efforts to conceive a correct plan of the premises.

274
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:08,200
Millcoat, Shire.

275
00:19:09,219 --> 00:19:11,520
I brushed up my recollections of the map of England.

276
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:15,579
Yes, I saw it, both the Shire and the town.

277
00:19:17,170 --> 00:19:21,940
Shire was 70 miles nearer London than the remote county where I now resided.

278
00:19:23,069 --> 00:19:24,739
That was a recommendation to me.

279
00:19:26,799 --> 00:19:29,200
I longed to go where there was life and movement.

280
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:34,000
Millcoat was a large manufacturing town on the banks of the earth.

281
00:19:35,659 --> 00:19:38,631
A busy place enough, doubtless, so much the

282
00:19:38,632 --> 00:19:41,739
better, it would be a complete change at least.

283
00:19:42,739 --> 00:19:45,297
Not that my fancy was much captivated by the

284
00:19:45,298 --> 00:19:48,761
idea of long chimneys and clouds of smoke.

285
00:19:49,159 --> 00:19:54,700
But, I argued, Thornfield will probably be a good way from the town.

286
00:19:55,579 --> 00:19:59,459
Here, the socket of the candle dropped and the wick went out.

287
00:20:00,319 --> 00:20:02,739
Next day, new steps were to be taken.

288
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:06,059
My plans could no longer be confined to my own breast.

289
00:20:06,739 --> 00:20:09,700
I must impart them in order to achieve their success.

290
00:20:11,319 --> 00:20:16,139
Having sought and obtained an audience of the superintendent during the noon tide

291
00:20:16,140 --> 00:20:20,709
recreation, I told her I had a prospect of getting a new

292
00:20:20,710 --> 00:20:25,059
situation where the salary would be double what I now received.

293
00:20:25,610 --> 00:20:28,719
For at low would I only got pound 15 per annum.

294
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:35,840
And requested she would break the matter for me to Mr. Brocklehurst, or some of the

295
00:20:35,841 --> 00:20:42,361
committee, and ascertain whether they would permit me to mention them as references.

296
00:20:43,190 --> 00:20:47,559
She obligingly consented to act as mediatrics in the matter.

297
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:54,323
The next day, she laid the affair before Mr. Brocklehurst, who said that Mrs.

298
00:20:54,324 --> 00:20:58,159
Reed must be written to, as she was my natural guardian.

299
00:20:59,190 --> 00:21:04,440
A note was accordingly addressed to that lady, who returned for answer,

300
00:21:05,389 --> 00:21:07,260
that I might do as I pleased.

301
00:21:07,979 --> 00:21:11,319
She had long relinquished all interference in my affairs.

302
00:21:12,989 --> 00:21:15,159
This note went the round of the committee.

303
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:20,406
And at last, after what appeared to me most tedious delay,

304
00:21:20,406 --> 00:21:23,579
formal leave was given me to better my condition if I could.

305
00:21:25,149 --> 00:21:29,586
And an assurance added that as I had always conducted

306
00:21:29,587 --> 00:21:33,959
myself well, both as teacher and pupil, at low would.

307
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:39,899
A testimonial of character and capacity, signed by the inspectors of that

308
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:42,920
institution, should forthwith be furnished me.

309
00:21:43,770 --> 00:21:49,399
This testimonial I accordingly received in about a month, forwarded a copy of it to

310
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:55,020
Mrs. Fairfax, and got that lady's reply, stating that she was satisfied,

311
00:21:55,739 --> 00:21:58,876
and fixing that day fortnight, as the period for

312
00:21:58,877 --> 00:22:01,739
my assuming the post of governess in her house.

313
00:22:02,879 --> 00:22:07,479
I now visit myself in preparations, the fortnight passed rapidly.

314
00:22:08,719 --> 00:22:13,100
I had not a very large wardrobe, though it was adequate to my once,

315
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:16,739
and the last day suffice to pack my trunk.

316
00:22:17,700 --> 00:22:20,819
The same I had brought with me eight years ago from Gateshead.

317
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:24,959
The box was corded, the card nailed on.

318
00:22:26,299 --> 00:22:32,260
In half an hour, the carrier was to call for it, to take it to Loten, whether I

319
00:22:32,261 --> 00:22:36,760
myself was to repair at an early hour the next morning to meet the coach.

320
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:43,299
I had brushed my black stuff, traveling dress, prepared my bonnet, gloves,

321
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:49,100
and muff, sought in all my drawers to see that no article was left behind.

322
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:55,000
And now having nothing more to do, I sat down and tried to rest.

323
00:22:55,959 --> 00:22:56,959
I could not.

324
00:22:57,690 --> 00:23:01,819
Though I had been on foot all day, I could not now repose an instant.

325
00:23:02,579 --> 00:23:03,579
I was too much excited.

326
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:08,799
A phase of my life was closing tonight, a new one opening tomorrow.

327
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:13,036
Impossible to slumber in the interval, I must watch

328
00:23:13,037 --> 00:23:15,959
feverishly while the change was being accomplished.

329
00:23:17,799 --> 00:23:22,600
Miss said a servant who met me in the lobby, where I was wandering like a

330
00:23:22,649 --> 00:23:27,020
troubled spirit, a person below wishes to see you.

331
00:23:27,985 --> 00:23:33,340
The carrier, no doubt I thought, and ran downstairs without inquiry.

332
00:23:34,069 --> 00:23:38,719
I was passing the back parlor or teacher's sitting-room, the door of which was half

333
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:42,360
open to go to the kitchen when someone ran out.

334
00:23:43,639 --> 00:23:47,379
It's her I'm sure I could have told her anywhere, cried

335
00:23:47,380 --> 00:23:51,340
the individual who stopped my progress and took my hand.

336
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,000
I looked.

337
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:59,540
I saw a woman attired like a well-dressed servant, matronly, yet still young,

338
00:24:00,420 --> 00:24:04,299
very good-looking, with black hair and eyes and lively complexion.

339
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:07,680
Well, who is it, she asked?

340
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:10,924
In a voice and with a smile I half -recognised,

341
00:24:10,924 --> 00:24:13,540
you've not quite forgotten me, I think, Miss Jane.

342
00:24:14,739 --> 00:24:20,219
In another second, I was embracing and kissing her rapturously, bessy, bessy, bessy.

343
00:24:21,350 --> 00:24:22,350
That was all I said.

344
00:24:23,280 --> 00:24:27,639
We're at she half laughed, half cried, and we both went into the parlor.

345
00:24:28,819 --> 00:24:35,360
By the fire stood a little fellow of three years old, in plaid frock and trousers.

346
00:24:37,049 --> 00:24:40,639
That is my little boy, said bessy directly.

347
00:24:41,670 --> 00:24:42,959
Then you are married, bessy.

348
00:24:44,229 --> 00:24:49,420
Yes, nearly five years since, to Robert Leven, the coachman.

349
00:24:50,340 --> 00:24:54,020
And I have a little girl besides Bobby there that I've christened Jane.

350
00:24:55,290 --> 00:24:56,620
And you don't live at Gateshead?

351
00:24:57,750 --> 00:24:58,750
I live at the lodge.

352
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:01,299
The old porter has left.

353
00:25:02,180 --> 00:25:04,540
Well, and how do they all get on?

354
00:25:05,139 --> 00:25:07,879
Tell me everything about them, bessy, but sit down first.

355
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:11,159
And Bobby, come and sit on my knee, will you?

356
00:25:12,209 --> 00:25:15,059
But Bobby preferred sideling over to his mother.

357
00:25:16,899 --> 00:25:22,388
You're not grown so very tall, Miss Jane, nor so very stout, continued, Mrs.

358
00:25:22,629 --> 00:25:23,260
Leven.

359
00:25:23,540 --> 00:25:26,239
I dare say they've not kept you too well at school.

360
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:30,185
Miss Reed is the head and shoulders taller than you are,

361
00:25:30,186 --> 00:25:33,399
and Miss Georgiana would make two of you in breadth.

362
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:38,000
Georgiana is handsome, I suppose, bessy?

363
00:25:39,139 --> 00:25:40,139
Very.

364
00:25:40,924 --> 00:25:45,700
She went up to London last winter with her mamma, and there everybody admired her,

365
00:25:46,290 --> 00:25:48,219
and a young lord fell in love with her.

366
00:25:49,139 --> 00:25:51,260
But his relations were against the match.

367
00:25:52,549 --> 00:25:54,020
And what do you think?

368
00:25:54,600 --> 00:25:59,459
He and Miss Georgiana made it up to run away, but they were found out and stopped.

369
00:26:00,729 --> 00:26:06,940
It was Miss Reed that found them out, I believe she was envious, and now she and

370
00:26:06,941 --> 00:26:09,959
her sister led a cat and dog life together.

371
00:26:11,059 --> 00:26:12,340
They are always quarreling.

372
00:26:14,139 --> 00:26:16,319
Well, and what of John Reed?

373
00:26:17,559 --> 00:26:21,020
Oh, he is not doing so well as his mamma could wish.

374
00:26:21,819 --> 00:26:27,260
He went to college, and he got plucked, I think they call it, and then his uncles

375
00:26:27,261 --> 00:26:29,899
wanted him to be a barrister and study the law.

376
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:33,120
But he is such a dissipated young man.

377
00:26:33,979 --> 00:26:36,020
They will never make much of him, I think.

378
00:26:37,280 --> 00:26:38,280
What does he look like?

379
00:26:39,090 --> 00:26:40,159
He is very tall.

380
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:45,780
Some people call him a fine-looking young man, but he has such thick lips.

381
00:26:47,180 --> 00:26:48,180
And Miss Reed.

382
00:26:49,379 --> 00:26:51,751
Misses look stout and well enough in the face,

383
00:26:51,752 --> 00:26:54,880
but I think she's not quite easy in her mind.

384
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:57,479
Mr. John's conduct does not please her.

385
00:26:57,899 --> 00:26:58,959
He spends a deal of money.

386
00:27:00,430 --> 00:27:01,899
Did she send you here, Bessie?

387
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:03,840
No indeed.

388
00:27:04,555 --> 00:27:08,899
But I have long wanted to see you, and when I heard that there had been a

389
00:27:08,900 --> 00:27:12,420
letter from you, and that you were going to another part of the country,

390
00:27:12,940 --> 00:27:14,540
I thought I'd just set off and get a look at

391
00:27:14,540 --> 00:27:17,341
you before you were quite out of my reach.

392
00:27:18,729 --> 00:27:21,540
I am afraid you are disappointed in me, Bessie.

393
00:27:22,420 --> 00:27:23,520
I said this laughing.

394
00:27:24,399 --> 00:27:27,540
I perceived that Bessie's glance, though it

395
00:27:27,540 --> 00:27:31,399
expressed regard, did in no shape denote admiration.

396
00:27:32,379 --> 00:27:34,159
No, Miss Jane, not exactly.

397
00:27:34,909 --> 00:27:36,319
You are gentile enough.

398
00:27:37,569 --> 00:27:41,579
You look like a lady, and it is as much as ever I expected of you.

399
00:27:42,139 --> 00:27:43,799
You were no beauty as a child.

400
00:27:45,180 --> 00:27:47,219
I smiled at Bessie's frank answer.

401
00:27:48,250 --> 00:27:53,100
I felt that it was correct, but I confess I was not quite indifferent to its import.

402
00:27:54,389 --> 00:27:59,860
At 18, most people wish to please, and the conviction that they have not an

403
00:27:59,861 --> 00:28:04,299
exterior likely to second that desire brings anything but gratification.

404
00:28:05,899 --> 00:28:10,659
I dare say you are clever, though, continued Bessie, by way of solace.

405
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:12,940
What can you do?

406
00:28:13,950 --> 00:28:15,040
Can you play on the piano?

407
00:28:16,459 --> 00:28:17,459
A little.

408
00:28:18,489 --> 00:28:19,530
There was one in the room.

409
00:28:20,340 --> 00:28:24,719
Bessie went and opened it, and then asked me to sit down and give her a tune.

410
00:28:25,420 --> 00:28:28,239
I played a waltz or two, and she was charmed.

411
00:28:28,979 --> 00:28:32,500
The Miss Reeds could not play as well, said she exultingly.

412
00:28:33,329 --> 00:28:37,059
I always said you would surpass them in learning, and can you draw?

413
00:28:38,555 --> 00:28:41,000
That is one of my paintings over the chimney piece.

414
00:28:43,100 --> 00:28:47,979
It was a landscape in watercolours, of which I had made a present to the

415
00:28:47,980 --> 00:28:53,680
superintendent, in acknowledgement of her obliging mediation with the committee on

416
00:28:53,681 --> 00:28:57,260
my behalf, and which she had framed and glazed.

417
00:28:59,549 --> 00:29:01,940
Well, that is beautiful, Miss Jane.

418
00:29:02,799 --> 00:29:08,139
It is as fine a picture as any Miss Reeds drawing master could paint, let alone the

419
00:29:08,140 --> 00:29:11,139
young ladies themselves, who could not come near it.

420
00:29:12,610 --> 00:29:13,690
And have you learnt French?

421
00:29:14,659 --> 00:29:15,659
Yes, Bessie.

422
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:18,159
I can both read it and speak it.

423
00:29:19,250 --> 00:29:21,139
And you can work on Muslim and canvas?

424
00:29:22,219 --> 00:29:23,219
I can.

425
00:29:23,989 --> 00:29:26,159
Oh, you are quite a lady, Miss Jane.

426
00:29:27,120 --> 00:29:28,120
I knew you would be.

427
00:29:28,680 --> 00:29:31,319
You will get on whether your relations notice you or not.

428
00:29:32,799 --> 00:29:34,440
There was something I wanted to ask you.

429
00:29:35,479 --> 00:29:39,180
Have you ever heard anything from your father's kinsfolk, the heirs?

430
00:29:40,350 --> 00:29:41,420
Never in my life.

431
00:29:42,659 --> 00:29:47,180
Well, you know Mrs. always said, they were poor and quite despicable.

432
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:48,940
And they may be poor.

433
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:52,840
But I believe they are as much gentry as the Reeds are.

434
00:29:53,850 --> 00:29:57,438
For one day, nearly seven years ago, a Mr. Air

435
00:29:57,439 --> 00:30:01,060
came to Gateshead and wanted to see you.

436
00:30:01,340 --> 00:30:04,000
Mrs. Said you were at school 50 miles off.

437
00:30:05,149 --> 00:30:08,860
He seemed so much disappointed, for he could not stay.

438
00:30:09,969 --> 00:30:13,074
He was going on a voyage to a foreign country, and

439
00:30:13,075 --> 00:30:15,899
the ship was to sail from London in a day or two.

440
00:30:16,930 --> 00:30:21,100
He looked quite a gentleman, and I believe he was your father's brother.

441
00:30:22,649 --> 00:30:24,819
What foreign country was he going to, Bessie?

442
00:30:25,909 --> 00:30:29,440
An island thousands of miles off, where they make wine.

443
00:30:30,059 --> 00:30:31,159
The butler did tell me.

444
00:30:32,620 --> 00:30:34,159
Madera, I suggested.

445
00:30:35,079 --> 00:30:36,319
Yes, that is it.

446
00:30:36,639 --> 00:30:37,799
That is the very word.

447
00:30:38,760 --> 00:30:39,760
So he went.

448
00:30:41,079 --> 00:30:43,979
Yes, he did not stay many minutes in the house.

449
00:30:44,500 --> 00:30:45,780
Mrs. was very high with him.

450
00:30:46,479 --> 00:30:48,879
She called him afterwards, a sneaking tradesman.

451
00:30:50,020 --> 00:30:52,120
My Robert believes he was a wine merchant.

452
00:30:53,500 --> 00:30:55,139
Very likely, I returned.

453
00:30:56,084 --> 00:30:59,799
Or perhaps clock or agent to a wine merchant.

454
00:31:01,430 --> 00:31:05,180
Bessie and I conversed about old times and hour longer.

455
00:31:06,159 --> 00:31:08,520
And then she was obliged to leave me.

456
00:31:09,100 --> 00:31:12,555
I saw her again, for a few minutes the next morning

457
00:31:12,556 --> 00:31:15,120
at Loughton, while I was waiting for the coach.

458
00:31:16,389 --> 00:31:20,013
We parted finally at the door of the Brocklehurst

459
00:31:20,014 --> 00:31:22,920
arms there, each went her separate way.

460
00:31:23,870 --> 00:31:26,620
She set off for the brow of Lowed fell to meet the

461
00:31:26,620 --> 00:31:29,500
conveyance, which was to take her back to Gateshead.

462
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:35,813
I mounted the vehicle, which was to bear me to new duties

463
00:31:35,814 --> 00:31:40,079
and a new life in the unknown environs of milk-coat.
